Subject: metal 0024: air2nir host diagnostics (AIR_FC_UNDEF, AIR_EVAL_ZERO, AIR_EVAL_PRINT, AIR_EVAL_SCRATCH)

Host only; air2nir is not part of the iOS build. All off unless the variable is set.
  AIR_FC_UNDEF=1      pass no function constants (each undefined), as the device does with
                      boot-arg sweetmetal_fc_undef=1 (0022)
  AIR_EVAL_ZERO=1     --eval fills every buffer with zeros (metaltest's CA quad binds zeroed
                      fragment buffers 0-5)
  AIR_EVAL_PRINT=1    --eval prints the folded shader
  AIR_EVAL_SCRATCH=1  --eval first turns scratch back into variables (nir_lower_scratch_to_var)
                      and folds with algebra: control flow only, not IEEE-exact values
Used 2026-11-22 to fold QuartzCore fixed_frag_lph_cph (RESEARCH_LEDGER, metaltest 18/19).

--- a/tools/mesa/air/air2nir.c	2026-11-22 11:42:48
+++ b/tools/mesa/air/air2nir.c	2026-11-22 11:42:48
@@ -36,6 +36,19 @@
 #include "air_module.h"
 #include "util/ralloc.h"
 
+/* host diagnostic AIR_FC_UNDEF=1: pass no function constants, so each is
+ * undefined (air.is_function_constant_defined false, value 0) -- what the
+ * device runtime does with boot-arg sweetmetal_fc_undef=1 (metal 0022) */
+static unsigned
+module_constants(void *ctx, const void *bitcode, size_t size, struct air_constant_value **fc)
+{
+   if (getenv("AIR_FC_UNDEF")) {
+      *fc = NULL;
+      return 0;
+   }
+   return air_module_function_constants(ctx, bitcode, size, fc);
+}
